# Rewritten 2026-08-28 as UTF-8. The previous version switched to UTF-16 partway
# through, so every pattern after the first few was stored with a null byte between
# each character and matched nothing. *.apk and *.zip were both inert - `git status`
# listed three APKs and jadx.zip as untracked, and a `git add -A` would have swept in
# ~274 MB. This repo has already been through one emergency history purge for exactly
# that (20,000+ decompiled files plus a leaked API key); do not rewrite this file with
# a tool that emits a BOM or UTF-16.

# --- build output ---
out/
out-*/
target/
build/
*.class

# --- decompiled / reverse-engineering artefacts ---
decompiled_source/
decoded_apk/
jadx/
jadx.zip
com.zodiacomputing.ourania*/
*.apk
*.zip

# --- IDE ---
.idea/

# --- python (langgraph_agents): 218 MB of venv around a few KB of source ---
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# --- local per-user state ---
# saved_charts.properties and saved_transits.properties are the app's saved charts. They
# carried real, NAMED birth records - the operator's and a third party's - and were tracked
# and public until 2026-08-30. Runtime state, never source. Untracked, kept on disk.
# settings.properties holds the operator's real natal date, time and birthplace.
# The repo is public. It is tracked from the initial commit with placeholder values;
# untrack it with `git rm --cached` rather than committing the real ones.
settings.properties
saved_charts.properties
saved_transits.properties

# --- backups ---
*.orig
# Windows Explorer's own duplicates. Ctrl-C Ctrl-V in a folder makes "X - Copy.java", and on
# 2026-09-29 six of them reached a commit - copies of CLAUDE.md, HANDOVER.md, error_log.txt,
# handover-stamp.sh and two generators. A stale copy of a document is the defect this project
# logs more than any other; a stale copy that git is tracking is that defect with a ratchet.
*- Copy.*
* - Copy
# Hand-made backups, taken before an edit and named after the day. The one that matters is
# settings.properties.backup-*: settings.properties is untracked because it holds a real birth
# date, time and birthplace and this repo is PUBLIC - and a dated copy of it holds the same
# data under a name no rule covered. Two of them were committed on 2026-09-29 and the branch
# was rewritten to take them out.
*.bak-*
*.backup-*
*.clobbered-*
# Windows folder metadata. Describes an icon and a view state, means nothing to anyone else.
desktop.ini

# --- run output kept beside the source ---
# Diagnostics writes a dated problem report; the regression harness writes its console to a
# file. Both are a record of one run on one machine and neither is repo content.
ourania-report-*.txt
out-reg*-console.txt

# --- external tooling, kept locally, never committed ---
# apktool.jar alone was 23.3 MB of a 27 MB repository. Ignore rules do not untrack
# what is already in the index, so these were removed with `git rm --cached` on
# 2026-08-31; the files stay on disk and the build pipeline still finds them.
apktool.jar
apktool.bat
cfr-*.jar
*.idsig
*.keystore
*.jks

# --- logs ---
*.log

# --- generator safety backups ---
# GenerateExtraBodies keeps a timestamped copy of extra_bodies.json before rewriting it.
# That copy is a local safety net, not repo content: 1.4 MB per run, and the corpus it
# duplicates is already tracked. The seven .pre-*.bak files above it predate this rule and
# stay tracked deliberately - they are the record of specific splices.
*.json.bak-*

# --- packaged app (build.ps1 -Jar / -Package) ---
dist/
